SUMMARY:MST Walker Knob Overlook/Balsam Gap - Route 128\, 8.5mi\, 2\,300ft
  FITNESS HIKE
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**NOTE: Carpool meeting spot moved
  to Folk Art Center\, lower/bottom parking lot.**\n\nAccording to the Mt. 
 Mitchell Park website\, this trail is now open. If not\, we'll do what we 
 did last time and backtrack to the Little Butt overlook. https://www.alltr
 ails.com/trail/us/north-carolina/mount-mitchell-state-park-trail\n\nCar po
 olers will meet in the intersection of the Blue Ridge Parkway and Elk Moun
 tain Scenic Highway\, near Bull Gap at 9:00am. The hike will start at the 
 Walker Knob Overlook on the Parkway. Please let the hike leader know where
  you intend to meet us: carpool spot (9:00am) or trailhead (9:30am).\n\nAn
 y rain cancellation or venue change will be made by 8:00am.\n\nOut and bac
 k hike. The trail elevates quickly and then undulates along a ridge of the
  Black Mountain chain. Expect to see lots of moss\, ferns\, and fungi. Som
 e of the trail is rocky\; some is soft moss and pine needle carpet.\n\nWe 
 will stop for lunch at the Allen Rinas overlook\, a rather prominent rock 
 outcropping with a great view over the Asheville watershed (see photo) nea
 r the 4mi point\, and turn around there.\n\nMore ambitious hikers are welc
 ome to continue the approximately one mile (and 350ft.) descent to Route 1
 28\, and turn around there.\n\nWe will be near 6\,000ft elevation and unde
 r forest cover for most of the hike.\n\nPACE: Fitness hikes proceed at a s
 teady BRISK pace adjusting for steepness of grade. PLEASE BE IN SHAPE AND 
 CAPABLE OF HIKING THIS DISTANCE WITH ELEVATION. This is not a hike for beg
 inners. If your interests include outdoor fitness hiking for cardio condit
 ioning and endurance join us.\n\nDOGS: Dogs are welcome as long as they ar
 e trail friendly.\n\nIF YOU SIGN ON THIS HIKE AND CHANGE YOUR MIND (EVEN I
 F YOU ARE ON THE WAITLIST) GO BACK TO THE RSVP LINK AND CHANGE YOUR STATUS
  TO FREE UP YOUR RESERVED SPOT.\n\nRelease of Liability:\nThe organizer of
  this trip is volunteer and is not a professional guide. The function of t
 he organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate 
 in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to ass
 ume all risks of injuries\, illnesses and damages arising from\, as a resu
 lt of and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledging that
  you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms\n\nThis is a 
 Level 7 hike.\n*Hike Levels:Level 1\; 300-600 feet elevation gain\; Level 
 2 600-900'\; Level 3\, 900-1200"\; Level 4\; 1200-1500' Level 5\; 1500-180
 0' LEVEL 6\; 1800-2100' Level 7*\; 2100-2400' Level 8\; 2400-2700' Level 9
 \; 2700-3000' Level 10\; 3000-4000' ULTIMATE HIKES\; > 4000'
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314701446
 /
