DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T130000
SUMMARY:Strawberry Gap 5.2 mi.\, 1\,200  ft. elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Sign up opens Sunday\, May 10th 
 @ 8:00 PM**\n\nThis is a somewhat strenuous out-and-back hike\, with nearl
 y all of the uphill being on the "out" part. We'll do a moderate pace of a
 round 2.3 mph\, with breaks as needed and a 15-minute snack/water break at
  or near the turn-around point. It's a typical walk in the woods for these
  parts (which is to say\, beautiful!)\, and the payoff at the top -- Blue 
 Ridge Pastures -- has a panoramic view of the surrounding mountains.\n\n**
 *Dog Policy:*** Sorry\, but dogs are officially prohibited on this trail.\
 n\n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they should join t
 he Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Alternati
 vely\, contact me in advance and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1" after yo
 u've made it onto the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, I may
  be able to add your guest.\n\n**CARPOOLING TIME & PLACE**\nThere's ample 
 parking at the lot by the trailhead\, but let's carpool anyway so that our
  large group doesn't fill it up.\n\nHere's a link to the [carpool location
  on Google Maps](https://www.google.com/maps/place/Food+Lion/@35.5253197\,
 -82.4138144\,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x8859f0403dcd4c65:0xd1ae595dd417
 bfc5!8m2!3d35.5253197!4d-82.4112341!16s%2Fg%2F1tdw45t5?hl=en&entry=ttu).\n
 \n* We'll meet **9:30 AM** at Food Lion parking lot\, 1350 Charlotte Highw
 ay (Rt. ALT-74) in Fairview.\n* Gather at the side of the lot **closest to
  the Highway**\, furthest from the store. Look for me and my silver Hyunda
 i.\n* We **depart Food Lion just after 9:30 AM**\, so please arrive before
  that time. It's about 10 minutes from there to the trailhead.\n\n**Direct
 ions from Asheville**\n\n* Take Alt 74 East toward Fairview.\n* From the i
 ntersection with I-40 and I-240\, you'll be on ALT-74 for 6.7 miles. Food 
 Lion is on the left.\n\n**Directions from Hendersonville**\n\n* US 25 Nort
 h to Fletcher\, right turn onto Cane Creek Rd.\n* In 8.7 miles\, turn left
  onto Alt-74\, Charlotte Highway\n* Food Lion is less than a mile on the r
 ight\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LISTERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly sign up if you 
 \\*TRULY\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status t
 o "Not Going" as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And 
 please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\nIf you're on the waiting list\
 , keep checking the evening before. Despite what I wrote above\, we always
  get last-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll monitor the National Weath
 er Service forecast for the hike area. If the forecast calls for a> 50% ch
 ance of rain or temps below 25\, I'll email cancellation messages by 7:30 
 AM.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you have any questions\, message me through Meet
 Up.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n**LEG
 ALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibl
 y\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsib
 le for their own safety and\, by joining a hike\, affirm that they have th
 e appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. H
 iking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organiz
 er nor Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate all risks or be responsible fo
 r your well-being. Participants assume full responsibility for any injurie
 s\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314700685
 /
