SUMMARY:Cove Creek\, Lanning & Daniel Ridge trails
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/WvuBwW7Wk
 pjixs828](https://maps.app.goo.gl/WvuBwW7Wkpjixs828)\n\napprox 7 miles\, 1
 200 ish feet elevation gain\n\nthis hike involves a good part of the Danie
 l Ridge loop\, the trailhead for which is currently inaccessible d/t FS475
  being closed at Cove Creek. so instead we'll head in on FS809 to ascend O
 ld Lanning Ridge trail\, then head down past the lower falls\, Daniel Ridg
 e clockwise along\, up\, and parallel to the river\, to the intersection w
 ith Farlow Gap\, then on to the intersection with Lanning Ridge\, left pas
 t the upper falls and back down to the trailhead.\n\nanticipate carpooling
  from the Pisgah ranger station. meeting there @08:30. specifics will be i
 n comments\n\nanticipated pace 2.5 ish mph\n\nwell-behaved dogs are welcom
 e!\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appropriate\, trekking poles are a
 n option. bring a snack as we'll take a break mid-hike. and plenty of wate
 r\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, show up or change your status. 2 ) 
 be sure you are in adequate physical shape to complete the event. 3) show 
 consideration toward all attendees. I hike for stress reduction and want t
 o keep it that way as much as possible\n\nLEGALESE\nThis Asheville Hiking 
 Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from th
 e meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affir
 m that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipmen
 t\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neithe
 r your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety no
 r eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event\, participant understa
 nds and agrees
